     I think nethack's usage is probably wrong, but not in
the way you suspected.  A grappling hook or grappling iron
is attached to a rope, and thrown to catch on something so
that that rope can be used for climbing.  A grapnel is also
a hook attached to a rope, but is used for hauling things
out of water or to anchor light boats.  NetHack's "grappling
hook" is actually supposed to be a grapnel, although I don't
think there's much point in changing its name now.

     The grappling hook was implemented as a substitute for
the fishing pole when various slash'em features got added to
nethack however long ago.  It was felt that a fishing pole
was too specialized an item to be useful.  Seems to have
been pointless, since the slightly more general grapnel gets
no use whatsoever....


